        <span class="story-chip"><span class="story-num">05</span> Unit Control Ledger</span>
        <h2>A real-time database of which unit is where.</h2>
        <p>Every action, receiving, transferring, selling or counting, maintains a record of exactly where every unit is, across the entire company. This is the Unit Control Ledger: a real-time database of which unit is in which location, when it moved, and where it's supposed to be.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>If a stock count reveals a discrepancy, an adjustment is recorded directly, and that adjustment is also logged on the ledger</li>
          <li>The result is a single source of truth for every unit in your inventory, from the moment it enters the store to the moment it leaves</li>
        </ul>
