          What makes Teamwork Commerce RFID different from competitors?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce offers a native RFID stack that runs from tag commissioning at receiving through transfers, counts and checkout. No third-party middleware required, and the reader hardware is yours to choose. Our RFID is native to the core logic: every transaction (receiving, counting, transferring, selling) operates by individual EPC, not just UPC.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What hardware do you support?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We keep a certified hardware list for clients, covering the devices integrated and supported with TW POS Pro, including Bluebird RFID handhelds. It is deliberately short, roughly one certified device per category rather than a catalogue, and there are no certified EAS gates on it today. We recommend certified hardware for full compatibility; if you want to use something not on the list, your Client Success team can advise on support.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can vendors pre-tag items, or do we need to commission tags in-store?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Both. If your vendor or warehouse ships goods already tagged, they scan straight into the purchase receipt. If not, Teamwork provides an integrated encoding workflow inside the purchase receipt document: define quantity, print and encode tags, affix them, then RFID scan to populate the receipt with individual EPCs. One step, no separate process.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

